  "lang": "en",
  "title": "Orange minivet",
  "extract": "The orange minivet is a brightly colored bird in the cuckooshrike family, Campephagidae.\nIt is found all along the Western Ghats and west coast of India and Sri Lanka.\nIt was formerly considered a subspecies of the scarlet minivet which is considered to have a wider distribution in eastern and northern India and South-east Asia. Its natural habitats are temperate forests, subtropical or tropical moist lowland forest, and subtropical or tropical moist montane forest. The orange minivet is a species resident in southern India and Sri Lanka, that feeds primarily on insects while foraging in mixed-species bird flocks or in small single-species groups.",
